"they appear: a whole paragraph or a word inside an English sentence. Noto "
"Naskh Arabic, the default, is the face KOReader gives Arabic books; Noto "
"Sans Arabic UI is the face of its plain-text windows; any font KOReader "
"knows can be picked (a font copied into KOReader's fonts folder appears "
"after a restart). None shows those letters in the window's own fallback "
"font. Hebrew and Devanagari have their own fixed faces, the ones KOReader's "
"interface uses."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:282
msgid "Latest Reply on New Page"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:285
msgid ""
"Open the newest reply on a fresh page: your question, the usage line and the "
"KOAssistant label stay on the page before, and the reply's first line opens "
"the page. Markdown chats get a real page break (older exchanges stay "
"compact; the break moves forward with each reply and never touches saves or "
"exports); Plain Text chats align the view so the reply's first line starts "
"the screen. Chat window only."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:290
msgid "Open Chats at Latest Exchange"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:293
msgid ""
"When opening a saved chat, jump to the newest reply instead of the top. "
"Replies always land on the newest reply regardless of this setting. "
"Independent of Latest Reply on New Page (that one changes the page layout; "
"this one changes where an opened chat starts)."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:298
msgid "Plain Text Options"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:304
msgid "Apply Markdown Stripping"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:307
msgid ""
"Convert markdown syntax to readable plain text (headers, lists, etc). "
"Disable to show raw markdown."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:314
msgid "Text Mode for Dictionary"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:317
msgid "Use Plain Text in dictionary windows whatever the View Mode."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:324
msgid "Emoji"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:335
msgid ""
"KOReader ships no emoji font, so the icons below show as empty boxes without "
"one. This row installs the bundled Noto Emoji font into KOReader's fonts "
"folder and enables it as a UI fallback font (KOReader restarts afterwards); "
"once installed, it shows a display test that turns the icons on."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:343
msgid "Emoji Menu Icons"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:346
msgid ""
"Show emoji icons (🔍, 📖) in UI buttons and status indicators. Needs the "
"emoji font (the Emoji Font row above installs it). If icons still appear as "
"boxes or question marks after a restart, turn this off."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:351
msgid "Emoji Panel Icons"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:354
msgid ""
"Show emoji icons on Quick Settings and Quick Actions panel buttons (🔗 "
"Provider, 🎭 Behavior, 📜 Chat History, etc.). Needs the emoji font (the "
"Emoji Font row above installs it)."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:359
msgid "Emoji Data Access Indicators"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:362
msgid ""
"Show emoji indicators on action names showing what data they access: 📄 "
"document text, 🔖 highlights, 📝 annotations, 📓 notebook, 📚 library, 📊 "
"reading stats, 🌐 web search, (🔍) smart retrieval; in a chat with Quick on, "
"⚡ marks the actions that take the Quick preset. Needs the emoji font (the "
"Emoji Font row above installs it)."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:369
msgid "Panel Alignment"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:374
msgid "Align Quick Settings"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:377
msgid ""
"Left-align button text in the Quick Settings panel instead of centering. "
"Also available from the panel's gear menu."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:382
msgid "Align Quick Actions"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:389
msgid ""
"Left-align button text in the Quick Actions panel instead of centering. Also "
"available from the panel's gear menu."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:401
msgid "Hide Highlighted Text"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:408
msgid "Hide Long Highlights"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:416
msgid "Long Highlight Threshold"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:437
msgid ""
"How much of the screen chat, artifact, translate, dictionary and quiz "
"windows take. Expanded leaves only a hairline around them (and keeps "
"KOReader's status bar visible while a book is open), which fits more text "
"but leaves less room to tap outside. Also on each window's gear menu. "
"Compact dictionary popups are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:452
msgid "Plugin UI Language"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:455
msgid ""
"Language for plugin menus and dialogs. Does not affect AI responses. "
"Requires restart."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:457
msgid "Match KOReader"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:495
msgid "Please restart KOReader for the language change to take effect."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:506
msgid "Chat & Export Settings"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:512
msgid "Auto-save All Chats"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:519
msgid "Auto-save Continued Chats"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:529
msgid "Streaming"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:534
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1614
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1712
msgid "Enable Streaming"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:541
msgid "Auto-scroll Streaming"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:545
msgid ""
"Off: a response fills the first page and stays there while the rest arrives. "
"You turn the pages as you read, and the finished chat opens on the page you "
"are on. On: the window follows the arriving text, and a step up stops it for "
"that response. Either way, the Autoscroll button in the streaming window "
"switches it for one response. A result that is data (an X-Ray being built) "
"is always followed."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:550
msgid "Keep Reading Position"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:554
msgid ""
"If auto-scroll is off or paused and you are reading while the response "
"streams, the finished chat opens where you were reading instead of at the "
"newest reply. In Markdown it opens on the page containing your spot; in "
"Plain Text your spot starts the view."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:559
msgid "Page-based Scroll (e-ink)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:563
msgid ""
"While the window follows a response in the plain text view: stream text into "
"empty page space instead of scrolling from the bottom. Reduces full-screen "
"refreshes on e-ink. Disable for continuous bottom-scrolling."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:568
msgid "Markdown While Streaming"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:576
msgid ""
"Show the answer rendered while it streams (bold, headings, lists, the fonts "
"of every script) instead of plain text swapped for the rendered view at the "
"end. It is drawn again several times a second where the device keeps up, and "
"less often on a slow device or as the answer grows, since each time the "
"whole answer is laid out again. Grayed out while Plain Text is your default."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:581
msgid "Large Stream Dialog"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:589
msgid "Stream Poll Interval (ms)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:596
msgid ""
"How often to check for new stream data.\n"
"Lower = snappier but uses more battery."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:602
msgid "Display Refresh Interval (ms)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:609
msgid ""
"How often to refresh the display during streaming.\n"
"Higher = better performance on slower devices."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:621
msgid "Quick Answer Preset"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:626
msgid "Quick Answer On by Default"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:629
msgid ""
"Start new chats with the Quick Answer (⚡) button already on. You can still "
"turn it off per chat: and override the default per book from Book Settings "
"or the ⚡ button's menu."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:644
msgid ""
"How strongly Quick Answer asks for brevity: Standard requests a short, "
"direct reply (a few sentences, no preamble); Ultra-brief enforces a hard "
"ceiling (at most 3 short sentences, one plain paragraph, never restate the "
"question); Off sends no brevity instruction."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:651
msgid "Turn Reasoning Off"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:654
msgid ""
"Disable model reasoning/thinking for Quick Answer chats (models that can't "
"disable it drop to their lowest level)."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:659
msgid "Turn Web Search Off"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:666
msgid "Turn Book Tools Off"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:673
msgid "Skip Domain Lens"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:676
msgid ""
"Leave the selected domain lens out of Quick Answer chats. Off by default: "
"the domain shapes identity rather than length, and costs almost nothing in "
"speed."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:681
msgid "Skip Book Background"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:684
msgid ""
"Leave the per-book Background note out of Quick Answer chats. Off by "
"default: the Background frames how you read this book, and costs almost "
"nothing in speed."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:694
msgid ""
"Optionally change the AI behavior while Quick Answer is on: keep the current "
"one (default), swap to its Mini variant (same style family when one exists), "
"pin a specific behavior (the built-in Terse suits Quick Answer), or send "
"none at all. Actions that pin a behavior are unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:716
msgid "Model override: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:718
msgid ""
"Optionally switch models while Quick Answer is on (that chat only: your "
"default model is untouched): the active provider's fastest listed model, a "
"tier of the active provider, or a pinned specific model. Custom providers "
"keep the current model unless custom_models.lua gives them tier placements. "
"A model picked for one run (a long press on Send) overrides it."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:733
msgid ""
"On by default: the AI is told not to reveal events beyond your current "
"reading position in book and highlight chats, and X-Ray checkpoint updates "
"follow your position instead of installing the newest version. Research mode "
"and a book marked Finished disable protection. Override per book in Book "
"Settings; per chat via the Spoiler chip (chat input's gear menu → Toolbar "
"Buttons). Custom actions can use the {spoiler_free_nudge} placeholder."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:740
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2039
msgid "Content Format"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:745
msgid "Export Style"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:752
msgid ""
"Markdown uses # headers and **bold**. Plain text uses simple formatting."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:761
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:776
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:792
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:808
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:828
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1587
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1603
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1733
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1749
msgid "Ask every time"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:767
msgid "What to include when copying chat to clipboard."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:782
msgid "What to include when saving to note."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:787
msgid "Save to File Content"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:791
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:807
msgid "Follow Copy Content"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:798
msgid ""
"What to include when saving chat to file. 'Follow Copy Content' uses your "
"Copy Content setting."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:803
msgid "Chat History Export"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:814
msgid "What to include when exporting from Chat History."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:822
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2066
msgid "Save Location"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:826
msgid "KOAssistant exports folder"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:827
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2072
msgid "Custom folder"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:836
msgid ""
"Where to save exported chat files. Creates subfolders for book/general/multi-"
"book chats.\n"
"\n"
"Default folder:\n"
"%1\n"
"\n"
"Custom folder:\n"
"%2"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:838
msgid ""
"Where to save exported chat files. Creates subfolders for book/general/multi-"
"book chats.\n"
"\n"
"Default folder:\n"
"%1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:854
msgid "Save book chats alongside books"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:857
msgid ""
"When enabled, book chats are saved to a 'chats' subfolder next to the book "
"file instead of the central location."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:869
msgid "Reading & Library"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:878
msgid "Chapter Quiz: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:885
msgid "Quiz on Chapter End"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:888
msgid ""
"Offer a comprehension quiz when you finish reading a chapter. Requires a "
"book with a table of contents."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:893
msgid "Quiz Chapter Level"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:903
msgid ""
"Which TOC level counts as a 'chapter' for end-of-chapter quizzes. A fixed "
"level falls back to the deepest level the book actually has. 'Auto-detect' "
"picks the deepest level whose chapters are at least the minimum length "
"below. 'All TOC headings' follows KOReader's TOC tick settings. Short or "
"skimmed chapters are skipped by the length setting below."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:909
msgid "Minimum Chapter Length (pages)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:916
msgid ""
"Skip the chapter-end quiz for chapters shorter than this many pages (0 = no "
"minimum). Also sets the threshold 'Auto-detect' uses to pick the chapter "
"level. Can be overridden per book in Book Settings."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:922
msgid "Minimum Reading Time (minutes)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:929
msgid ""
"Skip the chapter-end quiz unless you spent at least this many minutes "
"reading the chapter (0 = no minimum). Catches flipping quickly through a "
"long chapter. Uses KOReader's reading statistics; if those are unavailable "
"the quiz is still offered. Can be overridden per book in Book Settings."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:935
msgid "Question Count"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:942
msgid "Total number of questions to generate per quiz."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:947
msgid "Difficulty"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:955
msgid ""
"Easy: straightforward recall. Medium: comprehension and application. Hard: "
"analysis and synthesis."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:960
msgid "Include Multiple Choice"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:967
msgid "Include Short Answer"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:974
msgid "Include Discussion"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:990
msgid "Automatic X-Ray (all books)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:993
msgid ""
"Keep the X-Rays you started up to date as you read (flowing formats like "
"EPUB only): checkpoints at chapter-sized steps, always keeping the next "
"checkpoint ready ahead of you; reaching it installs it instantly and the one "
"after starts building. Books with no X-Ray are left alone: start one from "
"the X-Ray popup with \"In checkpoints, as I read (automatic)\", or switch a "
"book to Automatic individually (X-Ray popup or Book Settings → X-Ray → "
"Automatic X-Ray), which works even with this off; a per-book Off always "
"wins.\n"
"\n"
"Spend guards: a cooldown before retrying a step that was declined, failed or "
"cancelled, WiFi only, and the book's text allowed for the book, or a trusted "
"provider (a book on Ask is asked once); background runs extract book text "
"and use API tokens without a per-request tap. Leave off if every request "
"should be explicit."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1019
msgid "Cooldown (minutes)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1026
msgid ""
"Minimum wait before retrying an automatic checkpoint after one was declined, "
"failed or cancelled (0 = no cooldown). A completed build does not wait."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1032
msgid "Notify on Background Activity"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1035
msgid ""
"Show a brief notification when a background X-Ray update or create starts "
"and completes, and when a checkpoint is silently swapped in. Off = fully "
"silent (the X-Ray popup always shows the current coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1041
msgid "Checkpoints at Chapter Ends"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1044
msgid ""
"When building X-Ray checkpoints, place each checkpoint at the nearest "
"chapter end (within a few percent) instead of an exact percentage; "
"checkpoints then read as \"up to the end of a chapter\", and the versions "
"list shows the chapter names. Needs a table of contents. Checkpoint spacing "
"itself adapts to book length: about every 10% of a normal-length book, "
"larger steps for short ones."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1049
msgid "Preset for New X-Rays"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1052
msgid ""
"One tap for the three settings below it: the categories a new X-Ray tracks, "
"whether it keeps Current State (the section that says where things stand), "
"and how much each entry carries. Who's who is the shortest and cheapest (the "
"cast, one line each, no Current State); Characters only gives the cast a few "
"sentences each; Reference is the default (people, places, ideas and terms); "
"Everything adds the story arc; Light companion and Deep study change the "
"depth as well. Each setting can still be changed on its own; the preset then "
"reads Custom. A book can pick its own preset in Book Settings and a group in "
"its Group Settings. Applies when an X-Ray is created or rebuilt."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1057
msgid "Categories for New X-Rays"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1060
msgid ""
"Which categories a new X-Ray tracks by default: people, places, ideas and "
"terms unless changed here. The timeline (the story arc or the argument's "
"development) can be added, and people alone is the lightest. The last "
"checkbox, Current State, is the section that says where things stand "
"(Current Position in nonfiction, the Conclusion of a whole-book X-Ray): "
"every update rewrites it, so an X-Ray without it has shorter updates. "
"Applies when an X-Ray is created or rebuilt; individual books can pick their "
"own categories in Book Settings."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1065
msgid "Depth of New X-Rays"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1068
msgid ""
"How much each X-Ray entry carries by default. Light: one line per entry, "
"only recurring figures and turning points, about half the cost. Standard: a "
"few sentences per entry, everything the reader meets. Deep: longer entries, "
"every figure and development, richer connections. Applies when an X-Ray is "
"created or rebuilt; checkpoints and updates keep the depth the X-Ray was "
"started with. Individual books can pick their own depth in Book Settings."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1073
msgid "Type of New X-Rays"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1076
msgid ""
"Whether a new X-Ray uses the fiction schema (characters, places, story), the "
"nonfiction one (people, concepts, argument) or the academic one (concepts, "
"methods, findings, cited works). Auto, the default, lets the AI decide from "
"the work. Applies when an X-Ray is created or rebuilt; updates keep the X-"
"Ray's own type. Individual books can pick their own type in Book Settings, "
"which is where a book whose X-Ray came out as the wrong type is fixed."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1081
msgid "Carried Entries"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1084
msgid ""
"In a series or project group, entries from the group's other books that have "
"not appeared in the open book yet are carried along (in a series: from the "
"earlier books only). They always have their own list, \"Carried from earlier "
"books\". This sets whether they are also listed inside the X-Ray's own "
"categories, after the book's own entries, with the book each one comes from "
"beside it (the default), or on that list only. A group can set this for all "
"its books in its Group Settings, and a book in Book Settings. It changes the "
"lists only: nothing is sent and no X-Ray is rebuilt."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1089
msgid "X-Ray Entry for Matching Selections"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1092
msgid ""
"When a tapped word or selected text exactly matches an X-Ray entity's name "
"or alias, open that X-Ray entry directly, skipping ahead of the dictionary "
"and the highlight menu (including any bypass actions you have set there). "
"Anything that doesn't match falls through to your normal dictionary/"
"highlight behavior. Only does anything for books that have an X-Ray. A very "
"long press at the end of a selection always shows the normal highlight menu."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1110
msgid ""
"Discreetly underline words on the page that match an X-Ray entity's name or "
"alias, as you read (dotted gray, drawn shortly after the page settles; "
"entirely on-device). Tap a marked word to open its entry. Only active for "
"books that have an X-Ray. EPUB page mode only."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1123
msgid "Tap Marked Words to Open"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1126
msgid ""
"With passive marking on, a plain tap on a marked word opens its X-Ray entry, "
"like a link (real links in the text still win). Off = marks are visual only; "
"a long press still opens matching entries via \"X-Ray Entry for Matching "
"Selections\"."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1142
msgid ""
"Let marking, matching selections and entity cards recognize entities that "
"first appear past your installed X-Ray coverage, using only the next "
"checkpoint built past your reading position (never a later one). "
"Identification only: such names get short-dash marks and a card that, by "
"default, shows just the tapped name until you ask for the entry. Off = the "
"plugin only knows entities up to your installed coverage."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1157
msgid "Upcoming Entity Cards: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1163
msgid "Name only, tap to show a one-line description"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1166
msgid ""
"What the card shows first for an upcoming entity, known only from the next "
"checkpoint built past your reading position. Name only shows the tapped name "
"as written and its category; a tap on the card adds the entry's first "
"sentence, and another tap opens the full entry after a confirmation, "
"whatever the spoiler setting. First sentence right away skips the first "
"step. The confirmation box also offers Matching…, to stop a wrong underline "
"without reading the entry. Can be overridden per book."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1177
msgid "Card Shows: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1183
msgid "First sentence only"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1186
msgid ""
"How much of an entry the card shows for entities already in your installed X-"
"Ray. First sentence keeps the card to a one-line identification, with the "
"full entry a tap away. Full entry shows the entry's own text: its "
"description and what its page has under it, such as its other names and its "
"Significance (swipe to scroll it). Its connections stay on the entry's page. "
"Can be overridden per book."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1191
msgid "Entity Card First"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1194
msgid ""
"Exact entity hits (tapping a marked word, or selecting text that matches an "
"entity) open a compact card first: the name, category and role, and a one-"
"line identification, with the full entry a tap on the card away. An entity "
"known only from the next checkpoint built past your reading position goes "
"through stages instead (see Upcoming Entity Cards): its name, one line, then "
"the full entry after a confirmation, whatever the spoiler setting. Off = "
"open the full entry directly; an upcoming entity still goes through its "
"stages."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:1211
msgid "Footnote Panel"
